{"meta": {"limit": 100, "next": null, "offset": 0, "previous": null, "total_count": 36}, "objects": [{"abstract": "   This document specifies a new TLS certificate type for exchanging raw\n   public keys in Transport Layer Security (TLS) and Datagram Transport\n   Layer Security (DTLS) for use with out-of-band authentication.\n   Currently, TLS authentication can only occur via PKIX or OpenPGP\n   certificates.  By specifying a minimum resource for raw public key\n   exchange, implementations can use alternative authentication methods.\n\n   One such method is using DANE Resource Records secured by DNSSEC,\n   Another use case is to provide authentication functionality when used\n   with devices in a constrained environment that use whitelists and\n   blacklists, as is the case with sensors and other embedded devices\n   that are constrained by memory, computational, and communication\n   limitations where the usage of PKIX is not feasible.\n\n   The new certificate type specified can also be used to reduce the\n   latency of a TLS client that is already in possession of a validated\n   public key of the TLS server before it starts a (non-resumed) TLS\n   handshake.\n", "ad": null, "doc": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-oob-pubkey/", "expires": "2012-07-23T07:00:01Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 665, "intended_std_level": null, "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-oob-pubkey", "note": "", "notify": "", "pages": 10, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/dochistory/665/", "rev": "01", "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": "/api/v1/person/email/nomcom-chair@ietf.org/", "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/1/", "/api/v1/doc/state/150/", "/api/v1/doc/state/38/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "tags": [], "time": "2012-01-20T08:00:00Z", "title": "TLS Out-of-Band Public Key Validation", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "   This document specifies a new TLS certificate type for exchanging raw\n   public keys in Transport Layer Security (TLS) and Datagram Transport\n   Layer Security (DTLS) for use with out-of-band public key validation.\n   Currently, TLS authentication can only occur via X.509-based Public\n   Key Infrastructure (PKI) or OpenPGP certificates.  By specifying a\n   minimum resource for raw public key exchange, implementations can use\n   alternative public key validation methods.\n\n   One such alternative public key valiation method is offered by the\n   DNS-Based Authentication of Named Entities (DANE) together with DNS\n   Security.  Another alternative is to utilize pre-configured keys, as\n   is the case with sensors and other embedded devices.  The usage of\n   raw public keys, instead of X.509-based certificates, leads to a\n   smaller code footprint.\n\n   The support for raw public keys is introduced into TLS via a new non-\n   PKIX certificate type.\n", "ad": null, "doc": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-oob-pubkey/", "expires": "2012-09-12T21:35:33Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 2460, "intended_std_level": null, "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-oob-pubkey", "note": "", "notify": "", "pages": 10, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/dochistory/2460/", "rev": "02", "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": "/api/v1/person/email/nomcom-chair@ietf.org/", "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/1/", "/api/v1/doc/state/150/", "/api/v1/doc/state/38/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "tags": [], "time": "2012-03-11T21:35:33Z", "title": "TLS Out-of-Band Public Key Validation", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "   This document specifies a new TLS certificate type for exchanging raw\n   public keys in Transport Layer Security (TLS) and Datagram Transport\n   Layer Security (DTLS) for use with out-of-band public key validation.\n   Currently, TLS authentication can only occur via X.509-based Public\n   Key Infrastructure (PKI) or OpenPGP certificates.  By specifying a\n   minimum resource for raw public key exchange, implementations can use\n   alternative public key validation methods.\n\n   One such alternative public key valiation method is offered by the\n   DNS-Based Authentication of Named Entities (DANE) together with DNS\n   Security.  Another alternative is to utilize pre-configured keys, as\n   is the case with sensors and other embedded devices.  The usage of\n   raw public keys, instead of X.509-based certificates, leads to a\n   smaller code footprint.\n\n   The support for raw public keys is introduced into TLS via a new non-\n   PKIX certificate type.\n", "ad": null, "doc": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-oob-pubkey/", "expires": "2012-10-27T13:19:47Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 5698, "intended_std_level": null, "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-oob-pubkey", "note": "", "notify": "", "pages": 10, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/dochistory/5698/", "rev": "03", "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": "/api/v1/person/email/nomcom-chair@ietf.org/", "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/1/", "/api/v1/doc/state/150/", "/api/v1/doc/state/38/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "tags": [], "time": "2012-04-25T13:19:47Z", "title": "TLS Out-of-Band Public Key Validation", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "   This document specifies a new certificate type for exchanging raw\n   public keys in Transport Layer Security (TLS) and Datagram Transport\n   Layer Security (DTLS) for use with out-of-band public key validation.\n   Currently, TLS authentication can only occur via X.509-based Public\n   Key Infrastructure (PKI) or OpenPGP certificates.  By specifying a\n   minimum resource for raw public key exchange, implementations can use\n   alternative public key validation methods.\n\n   One such alternative public key valiation method is offered by the\n   DNS-Based Authentication of Named Entities (DANE) together with DNS\n   Security.  Another alternative is to utilize pre-configured keys, as\n   is the case with sensors and other embedded devices.  The usage of\n   raw public keys, instead of X.509-based certificates, leads to a\n   smaller code footprint.\n\n   This document introduces the support for raw public keys in TLS.\n", "ad": null, "doc": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-oob-pubkey/", "expires": "2013-01-17T17:30:26Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 9316, "intended_std_level": null, "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-oob-pubkey", "note": "", "notify": "", "pages": 12, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/dochistory/9316/", "rev": "04", "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": "/api/v1/person/email/nomcom-chair@ietf.org/", "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/1/", "/api/v1/doc/state/150/", "/api/v1/doc/state/38/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "tags": [], "time": "2012-07-16T16:30:26Z", "title": "Out-of-Band Public Key Validation for Transport Layer Security", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "   This document specifies a new certificate type for exchanging raw\n   public keys in Transport Layer Security (TLS) and Datagram Transport\n   Layer Security (DTLS) for use with out-of-band public key validation.\n   Currently, TLS authentication can only occur via X.509-based Public\n   Key Infrastructure (PKI) or OpenPGP certificates.  By specifying a\n   minimum resource for raw public key exchange, implementations can use\n   alternative public key validation methods.\n\n   One such alternative public key valiation method is offered by the\n   DNS-Based Authentication of Named Entities (DANE) together with DNS\n   Security.  Another alternative is to utilize pre-configured keys, as\n   is the case with sensors and other embedded devices.  The usage of\n   raw public keys, instead of X.509-based certificates, leads to a\n   smaller code footprint.\n\n   This document introduces the support for raw public keys in TLS.\n", "ad": null, "doc": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-oob-pubkey/", "expires": "2013-04-25T16:39:56Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 9326, "intended_std_level": null, "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-oob-pubkey", "note": "", "notify": "", "pages": 14, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/dochistory/9326/", "rev": "05", "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": "/api/v1/person/email/nomcom-chair@ietf.org/", "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/1/", "/api/v1/doc/state/150/", "/api/v1/doc/state/38/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "tags": [], "time": "2012-10-22T16:39:56Z", "title": "Out-of-Band Public Key Validation for Transport Layer Security (TLS)", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "   This document specifies a new certificate type for exchanging raw\n   public keys in Transport Layer Security (TLS) and Datagram Transport\n   Layer Security (DTLS) for use with out-of-band public key validation.\n   Currently, TLS authentication can only occur via X.509-based Public\n   Key Infrastructure (PKI) or OpenPGP certificates.  By specifying a\n   minimum resource for raw public key exchange, implementations can use\n   alternative public key validation methods.\n\n   One such alternative public key valiation method is offered by the\n   DNS-Based Authentication of Named Entities (DANE) together with DNS\n   Security.  Another alternative is to utilize pre-configured keys, as\n   is the case with sensors and other embedded devices.  The usage of\n   raw public keys, instead of X.509-based certificates, leads to a\n   smaller code footprint.\n\n   This document introduces the support for raw public keys in TLS.\n", "ad": null, "doc": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-oob-pubkey/", "expires": "2013-04-25T17:11:01Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 21471, "intended_std_level": null, "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-oob-pubkey", "note": "", "notify": "", "pages": 14, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/dochistory/21471/", "rev": "06", "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": "/api/v1/person/email/nomcom-chair@ietf.org/", "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/1/", "/api/v1/doc/state/150/", "/api/v1/doc/state/38/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "tags": [], "time": "2012-10-22T17:11:01Z", "title": "Out-of-Band Public Key Validation for Transport Layer Security (TLS)", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "   This document specifies a new certificate type for exchanging raw\n   public keys in Transport Layer Security (TLS) and Datagram Transport\n   Layer Security (DTLS) for use with out-of-band public key validation.\n   Currently, TLS authentication can only occur via X.509-based Public\n   Key Infrastructure (PKI) or OpenPGP certificates.  By specifying a\n   minimum resource for raw public key exchange, implementations can use\n   alternative public key validation methods.\n\n   One such alternative public key valiation method is offered by the\n   DNS-Based Authentication of Named Entities (DANE) together with DNS\n   Security.  Another alternative is to utilize pre-configured keys, as\n   is the case with sensors and other embedded devices.  The usage of\n   raw public keys, instead of X.509-based certificates, leads to a\n   smaller code footprint.\n\n   This document introduces the support for raw public keys in TLS.\n", "ad": null, "doc": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-oob-pubkey/", "expires": "2013-08-19T05:46:41Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 30982, "intended_std_level": null, "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-oob-pubkey", "note": "", "notify": "tls-chairs@tools.ietf.org, draft-ietf-tls-oob-pubkey@tools.ietf.org", "pages": 17, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/dochistory/30982/", "rev": "07", "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": "/api/v1/person/email/nomcom-chair@ietf.org/", "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/1/", "/api/v1/doc/state/150/", "/api/v1/doc/state/38/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "tags": [], "time": "2013-02-15T06:46:41Z", "title": "Out-of-Band Public Key Validation for Transport Layer Security (TLS)", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "   This document specifies a new certificate type for exchanging raw\n   public keys in Transport Layer Security (TLS) and Datagram Transport\n   Layer Security (DTLS) for use with out-of-band public key validation.\n   Currently, TLS authentication can only occur via X.509-based Public\n   Key Infrastructure (PKI) or OpenPGP certificates.  By specifying a\n   minimum resource for raw public key exchange, implementations can use\n   alternative public key validation methods.\n\n   One such alternative public key valiation method is offered by the\n   DNS-Based Authentication of Named Entities (DANE) together with DNS\n   Security.  Another alternative is to utilize pre-configured keys, as\n   is the case with sensors and other embedded devices.  The usage of\n   raw public keys, instead of X.509-based certificates, leads to a\n   smaller code footprint.\n\n   This document introduces the support for raw public keys in TLS.\n", "ad": "/api/v1/person/person/19483/", "doc": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-oob-pubkey/", "expires": "2013-08-19T05:46:41Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 31168, "intended_std_level": "/api/v1/name/intendedstdlevelname/ps/", "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-oob-pubkey", "note": "Joe Salowey (jsalowey@cisco.com) is the Document Shepherd", "notify": "tls-chairs@tools.ietf.org, draft-ietf-tls-oob-pubkey@tools.ietf.org", "pages": 17, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/dochistory/31168/", "rev": "07", "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": "/api/v1/person/email/nomcom-chair@ietf.org/", "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/1/", "/api/v1/doc/state/16/", "/api/v1/doc/state/38/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "tags": [], "time": "2013-03-18T22:13:19Z", "title": "Out-of-Band Public Key Validation for Transport Layer Security (TLS)", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "   This document specifies a new certificate type for exchanging raw\n   public keys in Transport Layer Security (TLS) and Datagram Transport\n   Layer Security (DTLS) for use with out-of-band public key validation.\n   Currently, TLS authentication can only occur via X.509-based Public\n   Key Infrastructure (PKI) or OpenPGP certificates.  By specifying a\n   minimum resource for raw public key exchange, implementations can use\n   alternative public key validation methods.\n\n   One such alternative public key valiation method is offered by the\n   DNS-Based Authentication of Named Entities (DANE) together with DNS\n   Security.  Another alternative is to utilize pre-configured keys, as\n   is the case with sensors and other embedded devices.  The usage of\n   raw public keys, instead of X.509-based certificates, leads to a\n   smaller code footprint.\n\n   This document introduces the support for raw public keys in TLS.\n", "ad": "/api/v1/person/person/19483/", "doc": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-oob-pubkey/", "expires": "2013-08-19T05:46:41Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 32996, "intended_std_level": "/api/v1/name/intendedstdlevelname/ps/", "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-oob-pubkey", "note": "Joe Salowey (jsalowey@cisco.com) is the Document Shepherd", "notify": "tls-chairs@tools.ietf.org, draft-ietf-tls-oob-pubkey@tools.ietf.org", "pages": 17, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/dochistory/32996/", "rev": "07", "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": "/api/v1/person/email/nomcom-chair@ietf.org/", "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/1/", "/api/v1/doc/state/13/", "/api/v1/doc/state/38/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "tags": [], "time": "2013-03-20T11:48:44Z", "title": "Out-of-Band Public Key Validation for Transport Layer Security (TLS)", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "   This document specifies a new certificate type for exchanging raw\n   public keys in Transport Layer Security (TLS) and Datagram Transport\n   Layer Security (DTLS) for use with out-of-band public key validation.\n   Currently, TLS authentication can only occur via X.509-based Public\n   Key Infrastructure (PKI) or OpenPGP certificates.  By specifying a\n   minimum resource for raw public key exchange, implementations can use\n   alternative public key validation methods.\n\n   One such alternative public key valiation method is offered by the\n   DNS-Based Authentication of Named Entities (DANE) together with DNS\n   Security.  Another alternative is to utilize pre-configured keys, as\n   is the case with sensors and other embedded devices.  The usage of\n   raw public keys, instead of X.509-based certificates, leads to a\n   smaller code footprint.\n\n   This document introduces the support for raw public keys in TLS.\n", "ad": "/api/v1/person/person/19483/", "doc": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-oob-pubkey/", "expires": "2013-08-19T05:46:41Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 33448, "intended_std_level": "/api/v1/name/intendedstdlevelname/ps/", "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-oob-pubkey", "note": "Joe Salowey (jsalowey@cisco.com) is the Document Shepherd", "notify": "tls-chairs@tools.ietf.org, draft-ietf-tls-oob-pubkey@tools.ietf.org", "pages": 17, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/dochistory/33448/", "rev": "07", "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": "/api/v1/person/email/nomcom-chair@ietf.org/", "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/1/", "/api/v1/doc/state/13/", "/api/v1/doc/state/38/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "tags": ["/api/v1/name/doctagname/need-rev/"], "time": "2013-04-16T14:07:17Z", "title": "Out-of-Band Public Key Validation for Transport Layer Security (TLS)", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "   This document specifies a new certificate type for exchanging raw\n   public keys in Transport Layer Security (TLS) and Datagram Transport\n   Layer Security (DTLS) for use with out-of-band public key validation.\n   Currently, TLS authentication can only occur via X.509-based Public\n   Key Infrastructure (PKI) or OpenPGP certificates.  By specifying a\n   minimum resource for raw public key exchange, implementations can use\n   alternative public key validation methods.\n\n   One such alternative public key valiation method is offered by the\n   DNS-Based Authentication of Named Entities (DANE) together with DNS\n   Security.  Another alternative is to utilize pre-configured keys, as\n   is the case with sensors and other embedded devices.  The usage of\n   raw public keys, instead of X.509-based certificates, leads to a\n   smaller code footprint.\n\n   This document introduces the support for raw public keys in TLS.\n", "ad": "/api/v1/person/person/19483/", "doc": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-oob-pubkey/", "expires": "2013-08-19T05:46:41Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 33449, "intended_std_level": "/api/v1/name/intendedstdlevelname/ps/", "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-oob-pubkey", "note": "Joe Salowey (jsalowey@cisco.com) is the Document Shepherd", "notify": "tls-chairs@tools.ietf.org, draft-ietf-tls-oob-pubkey@tools.ietf.org", "pages": 17, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/dochistory/33449/", "rev": "07", "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": "/api/v1/person/email/nomcom-chair@ietf.org/", "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/1/", "/api/v1/doc/state/13/", "/api/v1/doc/state/38/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "tags": [], "time": "2013-04-25T03:23:08Z", "title": "Out-of-Band Public Key Validation for Transport Layer Security (TLS)", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "   This document specifies a new certificate type for exchanging raw\n   public keys in Transport Layer Security (TLS) and Datagram Transport\n   Layer Security (DTLS) for use with out-of-band public key validation.\n   Currently, TLS authentication can only occur via X.509-based Public\n   Key Infrastructure (PKI) or OpenPGP certificates.  By specifying a\n   minimum resource for raw public key exchange, implementations can use\n   alternative public key validation methods.\n\n   One such alternative public key valiation method is offered by the\n   DNS-Based Authentication of Named Entities (DANE) together with DNS\n   Security.  Another alternative is to utilize pre-configured keys, as\n   is the case with sensors and other embedded devices.  The usage of\n   raw public keys, instead of X.509-based certificates, leads to a\n   smaller code footprint.\n\n   This document introduces the support for raw public keys in TLS.\n", "ad": "/api/v1/person/person/19483/", "doc": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-oob-pubkey/", "expires": "2013-08-19T05:46:41Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 38864, "intended_std_level": "/api/v1/name/intendedstdlevelname/ps/", "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-oob-pubkey", "note": "Joe Salowey (jsalowey@cisco.com) is the Document Shepherd", "notify": "tls-chairs@tools.ietf.org, draft-ietf-tls-oob-pubkey@tools.ietf.org", "pages": 17, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/dochistory/38864/", "rev": "07", "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": "/api/v1/person/email/nomcom-chair@ietf.org/", "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/1/", "/api/v1/doc/state/13/", "/api/v1/doc/state/38/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "tags": ["/api/v1/name/doctagname/need-rev/"], "time": "2013-04-25T03:23:24Z", "title": "Out-of-Band Public Key Validation for Transport Layer Security (TLS)", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "   This document specifies a new certificate type and two TLS\n   extensions, one for the client and one for the server, for exchanging\n   raw public keys in Transport Layer Security (TLS) and Datagram\n   Transport Layer Security (DTLS) for use with out-of-band public key\n   validation.\n", "ad": "/api/v1/person/person/19483/", "doc": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-oob-pubkey/", "expires": "2014-01-17T00:11:26Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 39069, "intended_std_level": "/api/v1/name/intendedstdlevelname/ps/", "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-oob-pubkey", "note": "Joe Salowey (jsalowey@cisco.com) is the Document Shepherd", "notify": "tls-chairs@tools.ietf.org, draft-ietf-tls-oob-pubkey@tools.ietf.org", "pages": 15, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/dochistory/39069/", "rev": "08", "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": "/api/v1/person/email/nomcom-chair@ietf.org/", "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/1/", "/api/v1/doc/state/13/", "/api/v1/doc/state/38/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "tags": ["/api/v1/name/doctagname/ad-f-up/"], "time": "2013-07-15T23:11:26Z", "title": "Out-of-Band Public Key Validation for Transport Layer Security (TLS)", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "   This document specifies a new certificate type and two TLS\n   extensions, one for the client and one for the server, for exchanging\n   raw public keys in Transport Layer Security (TLS) and Datagram\n   Transport Layer Security (DTLS) for use with out-of-band public key\n   validation.\n", "ad": "/api/v1/person/person/19483/", "doc": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-oob-pubke